# CODEOWNERS — inert for a solo repo, real protection the moment a second
# GitHub username joins the project.
#
# GitHub can require review from the listed owner(s) before a PR touching a
# path can merge (repo Settings -> Branches -> branch protection -> "Require
# review from Code Owners"). For a genuine solo repo this does nothing useful
# yet -- you can't meaningfully require someone else's review when there is
# no one else, and self-approval isn't real protection. Leave this
# commented-out until a second contributor (co-founder, contractor) actually
# has push access, then uncomment and list them for the paths that matter
# most: the harness's own gate/policy files and the CI workflows that read
# them, so a change to what counts as "reviewed" itself gets reviewed.
#
# Uncomment and adjust when that day comes:
# .harness/                    @your-second-contributor
# .github/workflows/           @your-second-contributor
# docs/COMPLIANCE.md           @your-second-contributor
